.\" Please adjust this date whenever revising the manpage.
.TH HOWDY 1 "November 27, 2026" "Howdy help" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
howdy \- Windows Hello style authentication for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B howdy
[\-U USER] [\-\-plain] [\-h] [\-y] command [arguments...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Howdy IR face recognition implements a PAM module to use your face as a authentication method.
.PP
Without \fB\-U\fR a command is for the user that runs it, and for the user that started
sudo or doas.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBadd\fR [NAME]
Add a new face model for a user.
.TP
\fBclear\fR
Remove all face models of a user.
.TP
\fBconfig\fR
Open the config file in the editor of $EDITOR, else in nano or vi, and restart the
authentication service.
.TP
\fBdisable\fR 0|1
Enable (0) or disable (1) Howdy.
.TP
\fBgui\fR
Open the configuration window (also started as howdy-gtk). With \fB\-\-force\-onboarding\fR it starts the setup wizard.
.TP
\fBlist\fR
List the face models of a user.
.TP
\fBremove\fR ID
Remove a face model of a user.
.TP
\fBrename\fR ID [NAME]
Give a model another name.
.TP
\fBset\fR [SECTION.]OPTION VALUE
Set an option of the config file. The section is needed if several have the option. Needs root.
.TP
\fBsnapshot\fR
Save a few frames of the camera to the snapshot directory.
.TP
\fBtest\fR
Test the camera and recognition methods. Only root may compare the faces, run it with sudo.
.TP
\fBversion\fR
Print the version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-U\fR USER, \fB\-\-user\fR USER
Set the user account to use.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR
Skip all questions.
.TP
\fB\-\-plain\fR
Print machine-friendly output.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show a help message and exit.
.SH AUTHOR
Howdy was written by boltgolt. For more information visit https://github.com/boltgolt/howdy
